{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790717843,"nonce":"WjJDT+T9BTSQtK/L8DWRWFX/hUA=","title":"Compare raw and boxed Dynamic type tokens by runtime ID","message":"When an `Array\u003cDynamic\u003e` type token was compared with the same type value passed through a `Dynamic` function parameter, `haxe_dynamic_equals` returned false because one operand was boxed and the other was a raw runtime type ID. The focused `DynamicTypeTokenEquality.hx` reproducer failed at `Int parameter`; the local comparison in the same file passed. Class IDs can also fit in a 32-bit slot, so the native box probe must reject that ID range before dereferencing it as a pointer.\n\nThe runtime now recovers an ID from an integer box, compares raw/boxed tokens by ID, and skips 32-bit raw IDs in the 64-bit box probe. The focused reproducer covers Int, String, Array, and enum tokens. TestReflect's equality failures fell from many to one before its separate trap-stub crash. All 83 authored regressions, runtime Clippy, and workspace fmt pass. The full tiered run scored 770/1094 with no status regressions; Issue4740 and Issue9764 moved to pass and stayed passing in five isolated reruns each, though their source paths do not establish which part of this runtime change caused the improvement.","files":null}]}